 offering because investor demand fell short. It is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, and its 2027 capex plan is up 18%. It has said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. So the equity shortfall is already forcing it to cut spending.\n- **Sector:** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Equity markets have been \"less receptive\" in Q3 2026.\n- **Debt is open, at a higher price:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, and its 2027 capex is up 12%. Utilities will have to lean on debt, which is a question for the debt-market nodes (n3 and n7).\n\nI found no data on valuations, the size of the combined equity gap, or any utility with equity already secured. Equity could reopen if conditions improve, and Pellham's deferral language implies that.\n\n**Implication for grid equipment demand:** Pellham's 2027 order cuts and substation deferrals are a downside risk. This cuts against n5's \"demand rising\" conclusion.","ttft_ms":1916,"type":"result","duration_ms":26376,"uuid":"4d63c441-4e34-475f-939a-aff6f00a07d5","ttft_stream_ms":1163,"time_to_request_ms":62,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":10,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":64,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":205,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":131,"process_rss_mib_result":206,"process_anon_mib_result":124,"process_peak_rss